From: ROCKNIX <https://github.com/ROCKNIX>
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: boot_mode: disable ADC-based download-key check

rockchip_dnl_key_pressed() samples SARADC channel 1 and treats a
near-zero reading (0-30, out of a 0-1023ish range) as "download key
held at boot", forcing the board straight back into BootROM download
mode via set_back_to_bootrom_dnl_flag()+do_reset(). This is meant as a
convenience shortcut for boards that wire a physical recovery/vol
button through a resistor divider onto that ADC channel.

All RK3326 handheld subdevices (a/b/c) currently share a single
generic U-Boot devicetree (CONFIG_DEFAULT_DEVICE_TREE =
"rockchip/rk3326-common-handheld", "devicetree: separate" in the boot
log) with no per-board differentiation available at this layer, so
this check can't be scoped to specific hardware via the DT alone.

On boards where SARADC channel 1 is wired to a real control (e.g. an
analog joystick X-axis, as in the vendor "gamekiddy-joypad" node's
joy1_x channel), a centered/idle reading sits well above the
near-zero threshold, so this never misfires. On the GKD Pixel 2,
which has no analog sticks at all, that same ADC channel is an
unpopulated/floating pin that reads near 0V - which lands squarely in
the "key pressed" window on every single boot, sending the board back
into download mode in an infinite loop before it can ever reach
extlinux/the kernel.

This is a non-essential developer convenience (the BootROM's own
maskrom entry via a physical key held at power-on remains completely
unaffected, since it happens before U-Boot ever runs), so disable it
unconditionally rather than trying to distinguish boards without a
per-board DT to key off of.

---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c | 34 +---------------------------------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 33 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
@@ -39,39 +39,7 @@
 
 __weak int rockchip_dnl_key_pressed(void)
 {
-#if CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(ADC)
-	unsigned int val;
-	struct udevice *dev;
-	struct uclass *uc;
-	int ret;
-
-	ret = uclass_get(UCLASS_ADC, &uc);
-	if (ret)
-		return false;
-
-	ret = -ENODEV;
-	uclass_foreach_dev(dev, uc) {
-		if (!strncmp(dev->name, "saradc", 6)) {
-			ret = adc_channel_single_shot(dev->name, 1, &val);
-			break;
-		}
-	}
-
-	if (ret == -ENODEV) {
-		pr_warn("%s: no saradc device found\n", __func__);
-		return false;
-	} else if (ret) {
-		pr_err("%s: adc_channel_single_shot fail!\n", __func__);
-		return false;
-	}
-
-	if ((val >= KEY_DOWN_MIN_VAL) && (val <= KEY_DOWN_MAX_VAL))
-		return true;
-	else
-		return false;
-#else
 	return false;
-#endif
 }
 
 void rockchip_dnl_mode_check(void)
